  "implementation": [
    "One world-owned RGBA32F Texture2DArray holds query vertices, decoded native normals, packed native vertex light inputs, original tile/cell data and admitted cliff/transition data. Integer fields retain their original row-major order in consecutive pages.",
    "Array layers use exactly the original terrain_cells dimensions, preserving hardware normalized-coordinate nearest filtering. A floor(uv*size) prototype disagreed at NVIDIA boundaries and was rejected.",
    "Static images come from retained CPU source arrays, not GLES array readback, which clamps float layers to RGBA8 in this runtime. Original water initialization order and dynamic roof/track textures are preserved.",
    "Remove the unused sector-only soft_sample function and soft_track_texture declaration from contact programs. Actual object/foliage programs use 13, 13 and 12 custom/global samplers, leaving native shadow unit 13 available on the tested Android renderer.",
    "Power-of-two cell dimensions specialize integer page addressing to exact masks/shifts. Other dimensions keep the general division path. The global shader cache keeps distinct raw sources, with per-map shifts bound as uniforms.",
    "Natural/cliff changes rebuild the same shared array resource; fade copies and world/option cleanup retain their ownership rules. Cover-only consumers keep the existing lazy geometry-only path."
  ],
